    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-art-intake.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Theme art intake",
      "prov:value": "> make skills for avatar theme ingestion (need 3 meeting certain formatting\n> constraints), return sucches or explnation of falire\n>\n> …make as part of docuemtn ingestion skill.\n>\n> — owner, 2026-09-20",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-art-intake.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every constraint was paid for",
      "prov:value": "| constraint | verdict | the incident |\n|---|---|---|\n| all three layouts | **refuse** | `landing-architecture` shipped laptop + card and **no mobile** from 2026-09-20 to 2026-09-24. `resolveThemeBackdrop` refuses an incomplete backdrop *wholesale*, so the theme renders with **no** art — not two thirds of it. |\n| distinct content | **refuse** | commit `1b62b57` delivered three files of which **two were byte-identical** (same digest, both 1,606,269 bytes): two distinct images for three named avatars. |\n| orientation per layout | **refuse** | a portrait crop is not a landscape crop scaled down. The quiet area the sticky's text sits in moves. |\n| a declared destination | **refuse** | commit `0301fbd2` put three PNGs at the **repository root**, undeclared, with spaces and commas in the names. No gate saw them: `check-declared-assets` walks declared→disk, and the root is not an instance. |\n| dimensions measured | *structural* | `landing-engineer` is declared 1672×941 where its siblings are 1671×941 — one pixel, copied from a neighbour. Intake takes bytes and **emits** the declaration, so there is nowhere for a retyped number to enter. |\n| weight and format | **report** | the arriving PNGs are 1.5–2.3 MB against ~100 KB webp. Heavy art still renders, so refusing it would block work over a bandwidth judgement. |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-art-intake.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Do not repair somebody's art",
      "prov:value": "`check:theme-art:check` was held back from CI for the same reason: it refused\n`landing-architecture`, and a gate added in the same change as the check would\nhave made CI red over art that was missing rather than over a regression\nsomebody just introduced. The portrait crop arrived on 2026-09-24 and the gate\nwent in with it — a refusal now IS a regression.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-art-intake.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reading the report",
      "prov:value": "**This one is general, and it has now been paid for twice.** The rule is\n   stated here because this is where it was first measured, not because it is\n   about art. Second instance, 2026-09-20: the first run of\n   `check-escaped-markup` found the landing-page defect it was written for **and**\n   two pages that are simply correct — `translation-support.html` documents the\n   path `&lt;section&gt;/&lt;block&gt;/…` and `md-authoring.html` quotes\n   `&lt;table class=\"md-table\"&gt;`, both inside `<code>`, which is how a document\n   shows markup to a reader. 19 findings; 6 were real. Blanking `<code>` and\n   `<pre>` regions took it to 6/6, and the exclusion is tested in **both**\n   directions, because a test that only checks the excluded case passes equally\n   for a check that never fires at all.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-art-intake.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reading the report",
      "prov:value": "So when you write a check and its first run lights up broadly, the first\n   question is *which of these are correct?* — not *how do I fix the repository?*\n   A check that fires on legitimate subjects is a check somebody switches off,\n   and a switched-off check is worse than none because it reads as coverage.\n3. **Warnings do not accumulate into a refusal.** Twelve heavy files are twelve\n   reports, not a failure. Weight is `ll11`'s subject."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-art-intake.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The structure this grows into",
      "prov:value": "The owner chose the axis on 2026-09-20, as **\"1 + 2, then specialized to 3\"** —\nthree levels rather than a choice between three options:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    }
  ]
